        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d36-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d36-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Lincoln P. Bloomfield of UNA/P (the Planning Staff of the Bureau of United Nations
                    Affairs).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d36-f2" n="2" xml:id="d36-f2-content">
                <p>The reference to “the regular conference” is not clear. The attachment (Dulles letter to Senator
                        Wiley) refers to the tenth regular session of the
                    General Assembly, although preparation for this meeting would not begin
                    ordinarily until 1954. The same would be true also of the projected 10th
                    anniversary commemorative conference to meet in San Francisco in 1955.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d36-f3" n="3" xml:id="d36-f3-content">
                <p>Not attached to file copy.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d36-f4" n="4" xml:id="d36-f4-content">
                <p>None printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
